paragraph_count: 6
paragraphs:
  - Theorem
  - "Let f be a continuous function on [a, b]. Then there exists c ∈ (a, b) such that:"
  - ∫ab f(x) dx = f(c) · (b − a)
  - This is the mean-value theorem for definite integrals.
  - Corollary
  - "For any non-negative continuous function f, the average value over [a, b] equals f(c) for some c in the open interval."
